            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Olivia Arnold"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I heated the milk on a sauce pan. Used a hand held battery operated whisk to froth the milk.",
            "datePublished": "2019-09-02T20:57:00.770Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Paula"
            },
            "reviewBody": "What to do when you don't have an espresso machine? I warmed the milk, frothed it with my magic frother wand, added a packet of Starbucks Via Italian Roast Coffee, added Madagascar Vanilla, and frothed some more. I added a little whipped cream and cinnamon on top. Mmmmm good!",
            "datePublished": "2017-03-16T13:14:27.083Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tammy Lynn"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I don't have an espresso machine, so I use 1/2 c milk to 1/2 c strong brewed coffee. I heat and whisk the milk on the stovetop (which I learned from this site). I only put 1 T coffee syrup in, and that was plenty sweet for me. I'd like to try some raw sugar on top of the foam next time, which another reviewer suggested.",
            "datePublished": "2016-05-28T20:37:45.773Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "House of Aqua"
            },
            "reviewBody": "You want to steam the milk before pulling the espresso shot to prevent the espresso from expiring. Typically I make this using 8 oz. of milk.",
            "datePublished": "2014-07-05T08:16:03.240Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Holiday Baker"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The first time I made this drink was quite a few years ago. I found a recipe on line to make my own vanilla syrup. The vanilla syrup is so easy to make and so much cheaper. I would only add 1 to 2 teaspoons. It is very sweet. Even now, I just prefer the milk and coffee. I have whisked the milk with an Aerolatte after microwaving it, warmed in a small pot with a whisk, and the way I currently do it with a Nespresso milk frother which keeps it the thickest.",
            "datePublished": "2013-07-05T15:25:13.930Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
